When you search:

Dependency Injection

The embedding is too general.

The retriever may not find the correct section.

A chunk is simply:

A small piece of a larger document.

Example:

Document:

FastAPI supports asynchronous programming.

Dependency Injection allows reusable logic.

Middleware executes before and after requests.

JWT provides authentication.

Chunking might create:

Chunk 1

FastAPI supports asynchronous programming.
Chunk 2

Dependency Injection allows reusable logic.
Chunk 3

Middleware executes before and after requests.

                 Chunk Overlap

Now another problem.

Suppose your document says:

FastAPI supports asynchronous programming.

Dependency Injection helps code reuse.

Middleware runs before and after requests.

Suppose chunk size is:

2 sentences

Without overlap:

Chunk 1

FastAPI supports asynchronous programming.

Dependency Injection helps code reuse.
Chunk 2

Middleware runs before and after requests.

Now imagine an important explanation starts at the end of Chunk 1 and continues into Chunk 2.

We lose context.


Solution: Overlap

Instead of:

Chunk 1

Sentence 1

Sentence 2
Chunk 2

Sentence 3

We do:

Chunk 1

Sentence 1

Sentence 2
Chunk 2

Sentence 2

Sentence 3

Notice:

Sentence 2 appears in both chunks.

This is called chunk overlap.
